From: TwinQuill contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve free(NULL) semantics in the TJS allocator

A syntax error can destroy an engine before its variant-array stack has
allocated storage. The stack destructor calls TJS_free(NULL), which previously
subtracted the allocation header from NULL and passed an invalid pointer to
free. Return before performing pointer arithmetic for a null allocation.

Tested-by: tests/test_krkr_tjs2_source_admission.py focused git-apply unittest; forced Android CMake configure; mapsKrkrScriptAndEncodingErrorsAndRecovers Android instrumentation.

--- a/src/core/tjs2/tjsConfig.cpp
+++ b/src/core/tjs2/tjsConfig.cpp
@@ -723,4 +723,5 @@
 void TJS_free(void *buf)
 {
+	if (!buf) return;
 	free((char*)buf - sizeof(size_t));
 }
